## 1. Largest of Three Numbers

### 🎯 Problem

Find the largest among three numbers.

### 💻 Code

```java
package p1;

public class LargestOfThree {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int a = 25;
        int b = 40;
        int c = 30;

        if (a > b && a > c) {
            System.out.println("Largest = " + a);
        } else if (b > a && b > c) {
            System.out.println("Largest = " + b);
        } else {
            System.out.println("Largest = " + c);
        }
    }
}
```

### 🖥️ Output

```text
Largest = 40
```

### 🔑 Important

To check whether `a` is largest:

```java
a > b && a > c
```

`&&` means **both conditions must be true**.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## 2. Smallest of Three Numbers

### 🎯 Problem

Find the smallest among three numbers.

### 💻 Code

```java
package p1;

public class SmallestOfThree {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int a = 25;
        int b = 40;
        int c = 15;

        if (a < b && a < c) {
            System.out.println("Smallest = " + a);
        } else if (b < a && b < c) {
            System.out.println("Smallest = " + b);
        } else {
            System.out.println("Smallest = " + c);
        }
    }
}
```

### 🖥️ Output

```text
Smallest = 15
```

### 🔑 Important

For the smallest number, use `<` instead of `>`.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## 3. Divisible by Both 5 and 10

### 🎯 Problem

Check whether a number is divisible by both 5 and 10.

### 💻 Code

```java
package p1;

public class DivisibleBy5And10 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int num = 50;

        if (num % 5 == 0 && num % 10 == 0) {
            System.out.println("Divisible by both 5 and 10");
        }
    }
}
```

### 🖥️ Output

```text
Divisible by both 5 and 10
```

### 🔑 Important

`%` gives the remainder.

If:

```java
num % 5 == 0
```

the number is divisible by 5.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

