## 9. Leap Year

### 🎯 Problem

Check whether a year is a leap year.

### 💻 Code

```java
package p1;

public class LeapYearOrNot {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int year = 2024;

        if (year % 400 == 0 || (year % 4 == 0 && year % 100 != 0)) {
            System.out.println("Leap year");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Not a Leap year");
        }
    }
}
```

### 🖥️ Output

```text
Leap year
```

### 🧠 Leap Year Rule

A year is a leap year when:

```text
Divisible by 400
OR
Divisible by 4 AND NOT divisible by 100
```

Examples:

```text
2024 → Leap year
2023 → Not a leap year
1900 → Not a leap year
2000 → Leap year
```

### ⭐ Interview Tip

Don't simply check:

```java
year % 4 == 0
```

because `1900` is divisible by 4 but **is not** a leap year.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## 10. Absolute Value Conversion

### 🎯 Problem

Find the absolute value of a number without using `Math.abs()`.

### 💻 Code

```java
package p1;

public class AbsoluteValueConversion {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int num = -25;

        if (num < 0) {
            num = num * -1;
        }

        System.out.println("Absolute Value = " + num);
    }
}
```

### 🖥️ Output

```text
Absolute Value = 25
```

### 🔑 Important

If the number is negative:

```java
num = num * -1;
```

Example:

```text
-25 × -1 = 25
```

Positive numbers remain unchanged.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

